@@section 2
@@title SQ-MELT perf: melt tick method against the G7.1 alternatives, 2026-11-17 ([plan_post_scratch_1115.md](../plan_post_scratch_1115.md) G7.1, G8; [melting.md](../melting.md) 2)
@@date 2026-11-17
@@jars creativecommon
@@sources feature_writeup/melting.md feature_writeup/plan_post_scratch_1115.md
@@text
@@text Queued for a later perf run (owner, 2026-11-17: G8 "the perf comparison of G7.1 is queued for a later run"). Method: `tools/perf` session with JFR and the perfBot players (memory `perf-suite-bot-players`). Only the built method exists in code; (a) and (b) are approximated by config, as noted in the row.
@@text
@@table
## SQ-MELT-P2 | melt tick method (G8) against (a) extra rolls and (b) extra random ticks: ms per tick and melts per minute
@group perf
@commands Two fixtures, each forceloaded with 4 perfBot players: a snowy taiga area (snow layers on the ground, spruce) and a frozen ocean area (ice sheet), each with a 16x16 field of magma blocks and a 16x16 field of lanterns placed into the snow and ice. Four 10-minute windows per fixture, fresh copy of the fixture each time: (G8) defaults (`meltTickInterval 200`); (control) `meltTickInterval 0` (random ticks only, the 2026-11-14 method); (a) `meltTickInterval 0`, `meltChance 1.0`, `snowLayerMeltChance 1.0` (stands in for 5 rolls per random tick); (b) `meltTickInterval 0` with `gamerule randomTickSpeed 15` (stands in for 5x random ticks to meltable sections; over-counts, every block ticks more). Record `forge tps` mean tick time, JFR share of `Melting.*`, and melts per minute (count of target blocks changed: `cdevtest count` of snow, ice and water at the start and end of each window)
@pass G8 within 0.5 ms per tick of the control and below (b); melts per minute of G8 at least 3x the control; JFR `Melting.onScheduledTick` plus `Melting.onRandomTick` under 2 percent of server samples; no `LevelTicks` growth beyond the targets in reach (scheduled tick count steady)
@fails G8 costs more than (b): raise `meltTickInterval` default or cap scheduling per source tick; report numbers to the owner either way (the G7.1 report)
@owner true

@@section 3
@@title SQ-MELT / CQ-MELT G11 and E1: slow tier from lava and magma, hot places, the End, no fire in the End, frozen decor, 2026-11-17 ([plan_post_scratch_1115.md](../plan_post_scratch_1115.md) G11, G12, E1; [melting.md](../melting.md) 1, 3; TODO `tooling/scratch-1115-follow-ups #20`, `#22`, `#9`)
@@date 2026-11-17
@@jars creativecommon
@@sources feature_writeup/melting.md feature_writeup/plan_post_scratch_1115.md development/creativeCommon/src/main/java/com/SaintAlfonzo/creativecommon/melting/Melting.java kubejs/data/creativecommon/kubejs/tags/melting_tags.js
@@text
@@text Creative Common built 2026-11-17 (lane C1, build/libs). Group A superflat, `gamerule randomTickSpeed 3` unless a row says otherwise. `[melting]` in `config/creativecommon-common.toml`: `meltTickInterval 100`, `slowLavaRange 2`, `slowMagmaRange 2`, `hotMeltTickInterval 20`, `endContactOnly true`, `endNoFire true`, `sluggishMeltFactor 0.25`. Nether and End spots: `execute in minecraft:the_nether` / `minecraft:the_end` with `forceload add` first (wait 30 s). Each case at least 12 blocks from the others. Supersedes SQ-PS15-22 (slow tier frozen) and fills SQ-PS15-08 (E1).
@@text
@@table
## SQ-MELT-11 | slow tier (G11): packed ice and cryosol melt within 2 of lava or magma, never from a torch; blue ice and permafrost only touching lava, one step down; salt as before
@group A
@commands Boot log: `[melting] tags:` line (lava only 2). On stone, one spot each: `minecraft:packed_ice` and `immersive_weathering:cryosol` with lava 2 away (a gap block of stone between), with magma 2 away, with a torch touching; `minecraft:blue_ice` and `immersive_weathering:permafrost` with lava touching, with lava 2 away, with magma touching; a `salt:salt_block` touching packed ice, cryosol, blue ice, permafrost. Probe each spot with `cdevtest state` every 60 s for 15 minutes
@pass lava and magma at 2: packed ice -> `minecraft:ice` (then water), cryosol -> `minecraft:dirt`; torch spots unchanged; blue ice touching lava -> `minecraft:packed_ice`, permafrost touching lava -> `immersive_weathering:cryosol`; blue ice and permafrost with lava at 2 or magma touching unchanged; salt: packed ice -> ice, cryosol -> dirt, blue ice and permafrost unchanged
@fails torch melts packed ice: findSource fire radius for the slow tier not 0; blue ice at 2 melts: lava_only tag empty (boot line) or reach not 1; nothing melts at all: the slow blocks do not random tick, so only the lava's or magma's own tick finds them (lava must random tick: check `sources scan on their own tick` count)
@draft runnable steps not written yet; the next runner writes them from @commands
## SQ-MELT-12 | Nether (G11): packed ice, cryosol, ice and snow melt on their own with no source; blue ice and permafrost only beside lava
@group A
@commands In the Nether on netherrack, far from lava (16+ blocks, no lava above or below): `setblock` `minecraft:packed_ice`, `immersive_weathering:cryosol`, `minecraft:ice`, `minecraft:blue_ice`, `immersive_weathering:permafrost`; a second `minecraft:blue_ice` with a lava source touching it. Probe every 20 s for 5 minutes
@pass ice -> air within about 1 minute (melt tick every 15 to 25 ticks, chance 0.4); packed ice -> ice -> air, cryosol -> dirt, each step within about 1 minute (chance 0.4 per tick, the slow tier too, owner 2026-11-17); the lone blue ice and permafrost unchanged; the blue ice touching lava -> packed ice (then melts on as packed ice)
@fails nothing melts: `onPlaced` hot path (packed ice has no random tick, it needs the placement schedule) or `hotMeltTickInterval 0`; lone blue ice melts: lava_only flag skipped in `isHot`
@draft runnable steps not written yet; the next runner writes them from @commands
## SQ-MELT-13 | arid, dry and tropical biomes (G11; dry added 2026-11-17): ice and snow melt with no source; packed ice and snow on blue ice stay
@group B
@commands Fresh normal world; find a desert (`locate biome minecraft:desert`), a savanna and a jungle; at each, away from any light source: `minecraft:ice`, `minecraft:snow[layers=8]`, `minecraft:snow_block`, `minecraft:packed_ice`, and `minecraft:snow[layers=8]` on `minecraft:blue_ice`. Control: the same set in a plains biome. Probe every 20 s for 4 minutes. Boot: Creative Calendar loaded (the hot tag reads its season tags)
@pass desert, savanna and jungle: ice -> water within about 1 minute, the snow stack loses one layer at a time and is gone within about 1 minute, the snow block gone; packed ice unchanged; the snow on blue ice keeps 8 layers; plains: nothing changes
@fails nothing melts in the desert: `#creativecommon:melting/hot` empty (Creative Calendar's `creativecalendar:seasons/arid`, `/dry`, `/tropical` tags, `melting_tags.js` biome event) or `getNoiseBiome` reads another biome at that height; plains melts: tag too wide
@draft runnable steps not written yet; the next runner writes them from @commands
## SQ-MELT-14 | the End (G11): every source melts only touching blocks
@group A
@commands In the End on end stone (forceload): `minecraft:ice` with a torch 2 away (lit), the same with a torch touching; `minecraft:snow[layers=8]` with magma 2 away and another with magma touching; `minecraft:ice` with a `salt:salt_block` touching; `minecraft:packed_ice` with lava 2 away and another with lava touching. Probe every 20 s for 5 minutes
@pass the ice with the torch at 2 and the snow with magma at 2 unchanged; the torch-touching ice -> water; the magma-touching snow gone at once on placement; the salted ice -> water; packed ice with lava at 2 unchanged, touching -> ice
@fails reach in the End: `endContact` not read (`level.dimension() == Level.END`) or `endContactOnly` false
@draft runnable steps not written yet; the next runner writes them from @commands
## SQ-MELT-15 | no ordinary fire in the End (G11): flint and steel, fire charge, setblock, lava spread refused; soul fire allowed; old fire goes out
@group A
@commands In the End (forceload), a survival bot or `execute as` a player: flint and steel on end stone; a fire charge from a dispenser at end stone; `setblock ~ ~1 ~ minecraft:fire` on netherrack placed there; a lava source beside planks for 5 minutes at `randomTickSpeed 100`; `setblock` `minecraft:soul_fire` on soul sand. Then `[melting] endNoFire = false` (restart), `setblock minecraft:fire` on netherrack, `endNoFire = true` again (restart), probe that block for 30 s. Overworld control: flint and steel on netherrack
@pass End: no `minecraft:fire` block ever appears (`execute if block` false after each), the planks never burn; soul fire stays; the old fire is air within 2 s of the restart's first tick; Overworld fire lights; no ERR naming `EndFireMixin` and no mixin apply failure in latest.log
@fails fire appears: `EndFireMixin` not applied (SRG `m_6933_`) or `refusesFire` dimension check; soul fire refused: the check reads a tag instead of `Blocks.FIRE`; old fire stays: the scheduled tick check in `Melting.onScheduledTick`
@draft runnable steps not written yet; the next runner writes them from @commands
## SQ-MELT-16 | magma-like blocks (G11): Molten Nether Bricks melt snow like magma
